## Tables Used in This Project

The tables useful for hospital operations analysis were selected and integrated into a consolidated dataset.

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Patient Table** | Used for patient details and demographics. |
| **Admission Table** | Used for admission, discharge, patient, department, ward, and disease details. |
| **Department Table** | Used for department names and department-wise analysis. |
| **Ward Table** | Used for ward details, ward types, and bed capacity. |
| **Bed Table** | Used for bed information and resource utilisation. |
| **Disease Table** | Used for disease names and disease categories. |
| **Billing Table** | Used for billing, insurance, and patient payable amounts. |
| **Employee Table** | Used for employee details and staff count. |
| **Staff Assignment Table** | Used for department/ward-wise staff allocation and shifts. |

---

## Data Integration

The selected tables were integrated using their common key fields.

The **Admissions table** was used as the primary transaction table, while the Patients, Departments, Wards, Beds, Disease, Billing, Employee, and Staff Assignment tables were connected through their respective identifiers.

### Main Relationships Used

| Key Field | Connected Tables | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `patient_id` | Patients and Admissions | Connects patient information with admission records. |
| `department_id` | Admissions, Departments, Wards, and Employee | Connects admission records with department and staff-related information. |
| `ward_id` | Admissions, Wards, Beds, and Staff Assignment | Connects patients, wards, beds, and staff allocation. |
| `bed_id` | Admissions and Beds | Connects admission records with bed information. |
| `disease_id` | Admissions and Disease | Connects admissions with disease names and categories. |
| `admission_id` | Admissions and Billing | Connects admission records with billing information. |
| `employee_id` | Employee and Staff Assignment | Connects employee details with staff assignments. |

